# The skill mirrors under concepts/patterns/skills/ must stay BYTE-IDENTICAL to the
# live skills at ~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md, which are LF. That byte-identity is
# the whole point — it is what makes drift detectable by a plain `diff`.
#
# Without this rule, core.autocrlf=true converts them to CRLF on checkout (measured:
# 180 conversions, +180 bytes on army-SKILL.md), so the drift check documented in
# concepts/patterns/skills/README.md reports DRIFTED on every fresh clone — a check
# that reads authoritative and returns garbage.
concepts/patterns/skills/*-SKILL.md text eol=lf
